      "text": "Location: Fremont, CA (SF Bay Area)<p>Remote: Yes<p>Willing to relocate: No<p>Technologies: Distributed systems, database architecture, F1&#x2F;Spanner, infrastructure scaling, technical debt triage<p>Résumé&#x2F;CV: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.linkedin.com&#x2F;in&#x2F;joebar&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.linkedin.com&#x2F;in&#x2F;joebar&#x2F;</a><p>Email: joe@barrera.org<p>Distributed systems architect. 30 years building infrastructure at CMU, Microsoft Research, Google. I help startups (10-100 people, Series A-C) avoid catastrophic scaling mistakes. I&#x27;d rather prevent your outage than debug it.<p>What I&#x27;ve built: Mach kernel at CMU under Rick Rashid. Research systems at Microsoft BARC (Gordon Bell, Jim Gray). 9 years on F1&#x2F;Spanner at Google. 4 USPTO patents in distributed systems.<p>What I&#x27;m good at: &quot;Your database architecture will fail at 10x scale, here&#x27;s why and here&#x27;s the fix.&quot; Technical debt triage with limited resources. Pattern recognition from decades of catastrophic failures. Currently thinking about LLM verification architectures and why static alignment is the VLIW of AI safety.<p>What I&#x27;m looking for: Fractional CTO or senior advisory role (20-30 hrs&#x2F;week). Series A-C, 10-100 people, real infrastructure problems."
